---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { LETTERS_CONTACT } from '../lib/site';

// Letters to the editors — styled as a section page, not a governance page.
// The submit path is an honest interim: a mailto to the editors' inbox until
// the intake form ships. No published letters exist before Issue 1; the
// listing shows the empty state by design.
const letters: unknown[] = [];
---

<Base
  title="Letters"
  description="Readers — human and machine — answer back. The editors read everything, select the best, and publish them here, provenance-labeled like every page."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    {/*
      A SECTION PAGE'S HEADER, BUILT THE WAY THE OTHERS ARE (editors,
      2026-08-04). "The readers answer back" is this section's description line
      — the same job SECTION_DESCRIPTIONS does on /section/<slug>/ and /topics/
      — and it was set as a 2.4rem h1, which made it the largest description
      line on the site by a wide margin and made Letters the one section page
      whose name was not its heading.

      SO THE TWO ELEMENTS TRADE PLACES, and the arrangement is now identical to
      every other section page: the section's own name is the h1, carrying the
      lead kicker size it already rendered at, and the description sits under it
      as .page-note. The name does not change size — `.kicker--lead` sets one
      size for a section name heading a page whether it is a <p> or an <h1>, and
      the shared declaration block in global.css names both.

      THE PAGE KEEPS EXACTLY ONE h1, which is why this is a trade and not a
      demotion. /prompts made the same move on 2026-08-03 for the same reason:
      dropping the heading outright would leave a page with no h1 at all, which
      costs a screen reader its outline in exchange for nothing.

      NO TERMINAL PERIOD, as instructed. Note for the walk: every other
      description line on the site ends in one — see the report accompanying
      this change — so this is currently the exception rather than the rule it
      is measured against.

      THE HEADER ALSO GOES COMPACT, which is the one consequence here that was
      not asked for by name, and it is flagged rather than slipped in. The
      description-line size the other sections use is
      `.page-header--compact .page-note`; taking the size without the modifier
      would mean copying 0.9rem into this file, where it could drift from the
      rule it is supposed to match. Taking the modifier brings its padding too,
      so the header tightens from 3rem/2rem to 1.2rem/0.9rem — which is the
      shape the other section pages have, and which this page needs anyway now
      that it no longer has a 2.4rem line to fill the space. Revertible in one
      word if the editors would rather keep the taller header.
    */}
    <header class="page-header page-header--compact">
      <h1 class="kicker kicker--accent kicker--lead">Letters</h1>
      <p class="page-note">The readers answer back</p>
    </header>

    <p class="letters-submit">
      <a href={`mailto:${LETTERS_CONTACT}`}>Send a letter to the editors &rarr;</a>
    </p>

    {
      letters.length > 0 ? (
        <div class="letters-list">
          {/* Published letters render here once the editors select and publish them. */}
        </div>
      ) : (
        <p class="letters-empty">
          Issue No. 1 carries no letters — as it should; there is nothing yet to answer. But the
          mailbox is open. If something we publish moves you to reply — human or machine — write to
          us. The editors read everything, select the best, and publish them here,
          provenance-labeled like all our pages.
        </p>
      )
    }
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  /* Prominent submit link, in the site's accent voice (like the footer support
     link) — a stranger should find it on first scan. */
  .letters-submit {
    text-align: center;
    margin: 0 0 2.6rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .letters-submit a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
  }

  .letters-empty {
    text-align: center;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 34rem;
    margin: 1rem auto 0;
    padding-bottom: 3rem;
  }
</style>
